<This is one of my gripes, too (although bear in mind that monsters killed by 
<other monsters don't give you any XP or treasure). But I haven't thought of 
<any good way to make it more reasonable. Ideas, people?

Sure.  Replace the ring of conflict by two other rings.

1) A ring of intra-species conflict: hives of killer bees or parties
of orcs fight to the last creature (as they happen to encounter each
other), who then turns on you, but a visit to a treasure zoo leaves at
least one of each monster highly interested in your well being.

2) A ring of inter-species conflict, which is worthless against a hive
or raiding party, but a treasure zoo's inhabitants fight until only
one species is left to take out its ire on you.

If I were writing the code, I sure wouldn't bother making it easy (or
even possible ;-) for the adventurer to find out which ring version
s/he has except by trying it out.  This would help maintain the spirit
of adventure so essential to the game.

I think this would reduce the power of the ring suitably while still
leaving each replacement ring a desirable item to wear.

